{
  "_comment": [
    "Installed at /opt/sandbroker/etc/sandbroker.json as root:root 0444.",
    "It holds NO secrets: vault names, token FILENAMES, ports and paths only.",
    "Safe for the agent to read, and reading it is how the agent learns what",
    "vaults exist.",
    "",
    "bind: leave null for unix-socket-only, which is the default and the",
    "tightest setting. Set it to a tailnet (100.64.0.0/10) or loopback address",
    "to also expose MCP over HTTP. The daemon REFUSES any other address: the",
    "HTTP surface is unauthenticated by design, so reachability is the whole",
    "access control."
  ],

  "op_bin": "/usr/local/bin/op",
  "keeper_bin": "/usr/local/bin/keeper",
  "keeper_state_dir": "/opt/sandbroker/var/keeper",
  "tokens_dir": "/opt/sandbroker/var/tokens",
  "socket_dir": "/opt/sandbroker/run",
  "alerts_dir": "/opt/sandbroker/var/alerts",
  "socket_group": "claude-broker",

  "bind": null,

  "ntfy_url": "http://100.85.183.28:8090/sandbroker-alerts",
  "ntfy_token_file": "/opt/sandbroker/etc/ntfy.token",

  "max_output_bytes": 1048576,
  "default_timeout": 60,
  "max_timeout": 600,

  "_vault_comment": [
    "backend picks the password manager: \"1password\" (the default, so every",
    "vault below omits it) or \"keeper\". token names the file under tokens_dir",
    "either way -- a 1Password service-account token, or a Keeper Commander",
    "config.",
    "",
    "For a Keeper vault, `vault` is a SHARED FOLDER PATH from the account's",
    "vault root, not a vault name: Keeper accounts have exactly one vault and",
    "the shared folder is the thing that is named and scoped. Everything in",
    "the folder, subfolders included, is in scope and nothing else is:",
    "",
    "    \"KeeperDev\": {\"vault\": \"Engineering/Dev\", \"token\": \"KeeperDev\",",
    "                  \"backend\": \"keeper\", \"port\": 8774}",
    "",
    "Commander logs in as a USER, so that scope is enforced by the daemon and",
    "not by Keeper. Give each Keeper-backed vault its own Keeper account; the",
    "README says why.",
    "",
    "require_unlock gates a vault: no secret from it is resolved until a human",
    "runs `sudo sandbroker unlock <Vault>`, and the unlock expires on its own.",
    "The enforcement is the filesystem, not code -- the marker directory is 0700",
    "and owned by the broker, so writing one needs root or the broker user, and",
    "typing that sudo password IS the approval.",
    "",
    "Only `run` is gated. list_items and list_fields return names, never values,",
    "so gating them would add friction without adding safety."
  ],

  "vaults": {
    "Dev":        {"vault": "312.dev - Dev",        "token": "Dev",        "port": 8770},
    "Staging":    {"vault": "312.dev - Staging",    "token": "Staging",    "port": 8771},
    "Production": {"vault": "312.dev - Production", "token": "Production", "port": 8772,
                   "require_unlock": true},
    "Infra":      {"vault": "312.dev - Infra",      "token": "Infra",      "port": 8773,
                   "require_unlock": true}
  }
}
